Apply the final MCI WaveOut client reset before joining the producer.

Wine MCIAVI_player invokes waveOutReset even after the completed header queue
has independently reset its client. WINMM_Reset always resets the stopped
client; Wine ALSA performs drop/reset/prepare. Native cleanup only dropped
the device, omitting this distinct reset on completion and cancellation.

Reset the configured client under its producer mutex before joining. Keep
the stop flag set so cancellation cannot resubmit caller PCM. Cleanup still
closes if reset/prepare fails, as MCI ignores the final WaveOut reset result.
This restores API ordering, not Wine's independent driver thread timing or
whole-output parity. Failed hardware setup is not a configured client.

--- a/dd2_native_movie_alsa.h
+++ b/dd2_native_movie_alsa.h
@@ -108,6 +108,12 @@
     if(movie_alsa.device){
         if(movie_alsa.mutex)SDL_LockMutex(movie_alsa.mutex);
         movie_snd_pcm_drop(movie_alsa.device);
+        /* MCI resets the client even after its completed header queue reset.
+         * Always finish cleanup when these final transport calls fail. */
+        if(movie_alsa.source){
+            movie_snd_pcm_reset(movie_alsa.device);
+            movie_snd_pcm_prepare(movie_alsa.device);
+        }
         if(movie_alsa.mutex)SDL_UnlockMutex(movie_alsa.mutex);
     }
     if(movie_alsa.thread)SDL_WaitThread(movie_alsa.thread,NULL);
